# .samignore — files kept OUT of the Lambda deployment artifact (B-15)
#
# IMPORTANT — read this before assuming it is a standard SAM feature:
#
#   AWS SAM CLI has NO native .samignore / .lambdaignore support for
#   zip-packaged Python functions. Verified against SAM CLI 1.162.1:
#     * aws_lambda_builders/workflows/python_pip/workflow.py exposes a
#       hard-coded EXCLUDED_FILES tuple (.aws-sam, .git, *.pyc, __pycache__,
#       .pytest_cache, .venv, ...) with no user extension point.
#     * `Metadata: BuildProperties` file exclusion exists only for the esbuild
#       (Node.js) workflow, not for python3.x.
#     * `sam build --exclude` excludes *resources* from the build, not files.
#     * grep for "samignore" across the whole samcli package: zero hits.
#   Because both v2 Lambdas use `CodeUri: .`, an unmodified `sam build` copies
#   the entire aws/ tree into each artifact — v1 modules, aws/tests/, every
#   test_v2_*.py, docs, Dockerfile, deploy.sh, samconfig.toml, template.yaml.
#
#   So this file is applied by us, not by SAM: aws/deploy.sh runs a prune pass
#   over .aws-sam/build/<Function>/ after `sam build` and before `sam deploy`
#   (see prune_build() in deploy.sh). `sam deploy` zips the built directory, so
#   pruning between the two steps genuinely changes what is uploaded.
#
#   Consequence: `sam build && sam deploy` run by hand (or `make deploy-*`)
#   bypasses the prune and ships everything. Deploy via ./deploy.sh (or the
#   Deploy v2 Backend GitHub workflow, which calls it) to get the exclusions.
#
# Pattern syntax (deliberately small and predictable):
#   foo.py        matches only a TOP-LEVEL entry named foo.py
#   *.md          matches only TOP-LEVEL entries ending in .md
#   dir/          matches a directory at any path prefix given, trailing / is
#                 required for directories
#   v2/test_*.py  a pattern containing "/" is fnmatch'd against the full
#                 artifact-relative path
# Patterns without "/" never descend into installed dependencies, so a bare
# "*.md" cannot strip READMEs out of site-packages.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tests — never executed inside Lambda
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
tests/
test_curation.py
test_doi_minting.py
test_globus_upload.py
test_preview_clone.py
v2/test_v2_*.py
v2/requirements-test.txt
v2/scripts/test_*.py

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# v1 (legacy) application modules. The v2 handlers are v2.app.main.handler and
# v2.async_worker.lambda_handler; nothing under v2/ imports any of these
# (verified: no static import, no importlib/__import__ anywhere in v2/).
# Leaving them in the artifact only creates generically-named top-level modules
# (auth, utils, status, submit, ...) on the Lambda sys.path.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
auth.py
automate_manager.py
dynamo_manager.py
flow_action.py
globus_auth_manager.py
globus_automate_flow.py
organization.py
source_id_manager.py
status.py
submissions.py
submit.py
utils.py
mdf_flow_info.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build / deploy / infra metadata. template.yaml and samconfig.toml describe
# the deployment itself and have no business inside the running function.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
template.yaml
samconfig.toml
deploy.sh
Makefile
Dockerfile
requirements.txt
.github/
.samignore

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docs and local dev / demo helpers
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.md
demo_mdf_v2.py
show/
v2/*.md
v2/demo_*.py
v2/demo_*.sh
v2/local_*.py
v2/local_*.sh

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / OS cruft that the SAM python builder does not already drop
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
*/.DS_Store
